-- Pairs (x, y) with |x² − d y²| below a bound: Dirichlet's approximation
-- of √d gives one with the bound 3d, and for a nonsquare d there are
-- arbitrarily many, since each pair keeps a positive distance |x − y √d|.
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
